From 470f96370f46ea6b77f400857cf3b95c9d1fbd05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:03:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: the header's Internet tooltip on every framed page

The amber LAN-names state and its tooltip lived on Main_ReaperDash.asp
only; every other page is framed in reaper_shell.asp, whose header had the
WAN pill but not the tooltip, the amber state or the landns data in its
poll. The shell now carries the dashboard's box (z-index 310, above its
sticky header), the WAN pill as the anchor, and the tooltip functions
verbatim; one painter for the first render and the poll (Connected if v4
or v6, jade / danger - the dashboard's colours, then netPaint() for the
amber state; without a WAN of its own the pill names the mode in steel and
nothing is bound); the poll adds reaper_landns_state and
wan_ipv6_network() to its request; focus leaving for the framed page
closes a pinned box, because a click inside the iframe never reaches the
shell document. Lean: tests/test_landns_check.py (shell wiring + a
verbatim diff of the shared functions), tests/test_shell_nettip.py (the
topbar code run under node for five states).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
